// smoke — the second kernel: fields in.
//
// The spray's ^ declares `samples $wind cell 0.5`; every tick the wind's
// deposit bag is rasterised onto a lattice over the spray's bounds, and
// `$wind grad at row.pos` reads the gradient there — toward the wind's
// source. A negative `lean` pushes the smoke away from it, so the column
// leans downwind and straightens when the caster is unmounted and its
// deposit has decayed. The cast the other way — `casts $dankness` — is
// declared on the ^spray too: one aggregate per tick, not a row's business.
spawn
gravity plane.drift.@self.gravity
$wind grad at row.pos | mul plane.drift.@self.lean | write row.vel add
perish
